+#### Editor language-level selection
+
+Clients may send a literal `initializationOptions.phpLanguageLevel` such as
+`"8.1"` or `"8.1.0"`. This session choice takes precedence over `[php].version`
+and Composer requirements in every routed project; it does not rewrite saved
+configuration. Omit it, use `null`, or send an empty string for Auto, which retains
+the normal saved-configuration/Composer/default policy. Malformed selections reject
+initialization without echoing their values.
+
+The server advertises `experimental.phpWorkbenchLanguageLevel`. The existing
+`phpWorkbench/activeTarget` query reports the applied major/minor version. A new
+selection requires a fresh initialized session; saved-profile and extension
+refreshes retain the editor's selection. Extensions keep their existing independent
+configuration policy.
+
